```cs
public virtual void Insert(int index, Object value)
{
    Debug.Assert(index >= 0 && index <= _size, "SR.ArgumentOutOfRange_ArrayListInsert");

    // @@@ Check that the capacity is either the same as the previous or is increased by 1
    if (_size == _items.Length) EnsureCapacity(_size + 1);
    if (index < _size)
    {
        Array.Copy(_items, index, _items, index + 1, _size - index);
    }
    _items[index] = value;
    _size++;
    _version++;
}
```

This assert statement checks whether the capacity is either the same or increased by 1 after inserting the element at the given index.

```cs
public virtual int LastIndexOf(Object value)
{
    Debug.Assert(RET == -1 || RET >= _size, "The array list must not have an element with the value x if the return value is -1");
    return LastIndexOf(value, _size - 1, _size);
}
```

This assert statement checks whether the function returns -1 or a value that is not less than the size of the list. This means that the value is either not in the list (then the function returns -1) or it is in the list and its index is not less than the size of the list.
