The comment "@@@ Size of the list is equal to its capacity" refers to the initial capacity of the list being equal to its size at the beginning of the `Add` method. The capacity of the list starts at 0 and increases by 1 each time an element is added to the list. This ensures that the list will not repeatedly resize itself for frequent additions.
